#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: rust-type-pattern-on-a-local-val-matches-anything
description: "on the rust lane a Map type pattern matches a JSON ARRAY when the scrutinee is a local val; the same match on a parameter is correct"
---
# A type pattern on a local `val` matches anything (rust lane)

Reported from rozum, where it cost a working server for an afternoon. A reader that accepts
either `[...]` or `{"rooms": [...]}` took the OBJECT branch for an array, found no key, and
answered "no such room" for every room in a file that plainly listed them. Nothing failed — the
answer was simply wrong, so it reached production and was found by comparing two implementations
byte for byte.

**The discriminator is where the matched value comes from, and nothing else.** The two functions
below have identical match expressions. `viaParam` matches a parameter and is correct on both
lanes. `viaLocal` matches a local `val` and, on the rust lane, takes the `Map` arm for an array.

It does not depend on where the JSON came from: a literal and a file behave the same. It also
holds when the `Map` arm actually USES its binding, which is what made the wrong answer look
plausible — `m.get("rooms")` on an array simply returns nothing.

```scalascript
[jsonParse](std/json.ssc)

def viaParam(v: Any): String =
  v match
    case m: Map[String, Any] => "MAP arm"
    case other               => "catch-all arm"

def viaLocal(): String =
  val parsed = jsonParse("[{\"name\":\"a\"}]")
  parsed match
    case m: Map[String, Any] => "MAP arm"
    case other               => "catch-all arm"

def viaLocalUsingTheBinding(): String =
  val parsed = jsonParse("[{\"name\":\"a\"}]")
  parsed match
    case m: Map[String, Any] => m.get("rooms").map(v => "MAP with key").getOrElse("MAP, no key")
    case other               => "catch-all arm"

def main(): Unit =
  println("array via parameter : " + viaParam(jsonParse("[{\"name\":\"a\"}]")))
  println("array via local val : " + viaLocal())
  println("array, binding used : " + viaLocalUsingTheBinding())
  println("object via parameter: " + viaParam(jsonParse("{\"name\":\"a\"}")))
```

Measured with `bin/ssc` and `bin/ssc-tools build-rust` from the same tree:

```text
interpreter                      rust lane
array via parameter : catch-all  array via parameter : catch-all
array via local val : catch-all  array via local val : MAP arm      ← wrong
array, binding used : catch-all  array, binding used : MAP, no key  ← wrong
object via parameter: MAP arm    object via parameter: MAP arm
```

Expected on every lane: an array never takes the `Map` arm.
